<BaseLayout
  title="Editorial Team | wrongfulterminationcalc.com"
  description="Meet the editorial team behind WrongfulTerminationCalc — employment law and HR compliance experts who review every piece of content."
>

  <h1>Our Editorial Team</h1>

  <p>
    Every article, guide, and calculator on WrongfulTerminationCalc is written or reviewed by our editorial team before publication. Our team includes practicing attorneys and certified HR professionals with direct experience in employment law, wrongful termination investigations, and workplace compliance. We do not publish content that has not been reviewed for legal and factual accuracy.
  </p>

  <h2>Lena Hartfield, JD — Editor-in-Chief &amp; Employment Law Practice Lead</h2>
  <p>
    Lena Hartfield serves as Editor-in-Chief and leads the employment law coverage at WrongfulTerminationCalc. She earned her JD with a concentration in employment and labor law and spent over a decade advising both employees and employers on discrimination, retaliation, and wrongful termination claims under Title VII, the ADA, the ADEA, and parallel state statutes.
  </p>
  <p>
    Lena's practice background includes representing plaintiffs in federal district court proceedings, advising HR departments on compliant termination procedures, and conducting workplace investigations for mid-size employers. Her editorial work focuses on translating complex statutory and case-law concepts into accurate, accessible guidance for employees trying to understand their rights.
  </p>
  <p>
    Lena reviews all calculator methodology, legal claim-type descriptions, and any content touching on specific statutory rights or remedies. Her goal is to ensure that every piece of content on this site is legally accurate, appropriately caveated, and genuinely useful to the workers who need it most.
  </p>

  <h2>Nora Ferris, SHRM-SCP — Contributing Writer, HR Compliance &amp; Wrongful Termination Claims</h2>
  <p>
    Nora Ferris is a contributing writer specializing in HR compliance and the employer-side dynamics of wrongful termination claims. She holds the Senior Certified Professional (SHRM-SCP) credential from the Society for Human Resource Management and has spent her career embedded in HR departments at companies ranging from regional mid-market firms to large national employers.
  </p>
  <p>
    Nora's work focuses on the procedural side of terminations: how progressive discipline policies should be documented, what investigation records matter in litigation, and how employers' HR failures translate into employee legal rights. Her contributions include guides on recognizing red flags in termination decisions, understanding employer defenses, and navigating the documentation process after a disputed firing.
  </p>
  <p>
    Nora's SHRM-SCP credential reflects deep expertise in employment law compliance, workforce planning, and HR risk management. Her practitioner perspective adds an important counterbalance to legal analysis — understanding how termination decisions actually get made inside organizations is essential for employees evaluating whether their firing was pretextual.
  </p>

  <h2>Editorial Standards</h2>
  <p>
    WrongfulTerminationCalc follows strict editorial standards to maintain accuracy and independence:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>All legal content is reviewed by at least one attorney with employment law experience before publication.</li>
    <li>Statutory information, case citations, and EEOC data are verified against primary sources.</li>
    <li>Content is updated when significant legal developments (new statutes, major court decisions, regulatory changes) affect accuracy.</li>
    <li>We do not accept payment to alter editorial content. Our monetization is through display advertising only.</li>
    <li>We clearly distinguish between factual information and educational estimates. Our calculator results are estimates, not legal advice.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    If you believe any content on this site contains an error, please <a href="/contact">contact us</a>. We take accuracy seriously and correct verified errors promptly.
  </p>

</BaseLayout>
